{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>\"and let us see what will become of his dreams\"</b> This is a figurative expression spoken in mockery: let us see after his death whether we will bow down to him. But the correct interpretation in my eyes is that they said, \"Now let us see what will become of his dreams,\" meaning: if he is rescued from our hands, he will surely reign over us. But our Sages said (there), the Holy Spirit speaks: \"let us see what will become of his dreams\" — that is to say, whose word will stand, mine or theirs."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:41:10.769596746Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}